    "heading": "Warming Up With Some Simple Math",
    "body": "Hey everyone! I hope you are having a lovely morning. I just sat down with my coffee and dove into today's easy Pips puzzle. It was a great little brain teaser to get the gears turning. I started by looking for the most obvious spots where the dominoes could fit. The sum targets are always the best place to begin. For instance, in the top left, I saw that cell [0,1] was marked as empty while cell [0,2] had a target sum of 1. Looking at our domino list, the [0,1] domino was the perfect fit for those two spots.\n\nAfter that, I moved down to the bottom left. There is a sum target of 5 at cell [3,0] and an empty spot at [2,0]. The only domino we have with a 5 is the [1,5] piece, so I plopped that right in. It is such a satisfying feeling when the pieces just click into place like that! I followed the same logic for the rest of the board, matching the [2,2] domino to the sum 2 target at [0,3] and using the [3,4] domino for that target 3 at [2,3].\n\nThe trickiest part was deciding where to put the [1,4] domino, but since the only target left was a 4 at [3,2], it had to go there. By leaving the empty cells for the other half of each domino, the whole board cleared up in no time. If you were stuck, just remember that those empty regions are your best friends because they don't limit your options as much as the sum targets do!",
